@@ -70,6 +70,19 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to print and log. It converts each object to a string with plain string conversion and writes the result as raw text.
+
+``out`` does not pretty print, wrap, crop, apply markup, or replace emoji codes. Output is written as-is, with the separator and end string applied as given.
+
+``out`` does apply highlighting by default, and it accepts a basic ``style`` argument. Pass ``highlight=False`` to turn highlighting off, or ``highlight=None`` to use the console's highlight setting.
+
+    >>> console.out("[bold]Hello[/bold]", "World :smile:")
+    [bold]Hello[/bold] World :smile:
+
+
